{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nr=Path(Path('.game-path').read_text());title='Trauma Refrain: Third Opinion'\nmetadata={\n'sourceInformation':{'date':'2026-11-05 01:50:57','source':'Trauma Center: Second Opinion','plan':'PLAN.md','genre':'Surgical action; visual-novel drama; cooperative arcade simulation','perspective':'Fixed surgeon-eye 3D operative field with mild perspective; frontal paper theatre for story','tech':'Pavilion engine 0.1.0 at 49ef2ba, Rust 1.98.1, WebAssembly, wgpu 30, glam 0.33, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129; HTML/CSS/JavaScript shell and Web Audio','artDirection':'Original procedural cel-shaded medical illustrations, steel instruments, teal drapes, violet organisms, extruded paper characters; Barlow Condensed Semibold','animation':'Pavilion sim-driven procedural animation: heartbeat tissue, articulated instruments, spline-card acting, parasites, particles and score stamps','audio':'Original synthesized melodies, heartbeat-coupled score, procedural effects and Animalese-style formant voices; music defaults to 10%; no audio files','online':'AI Hub Session Protocol v1 shared-world Code Blue for 1–4 players, host authority, mirrored snapshots, local controller co-op','testing':'Headless deterministic simulation and browser scripts; scripted campaign, idle-loss, replay, inputs, UI, audio, responsive screenshots and hub harness; no physical controller, real iOS or second human','research':'Research supplied by PLAN.md on the 2006 Wii source; read Pavilion START_HERE.md, MAKE_A_GAME.md and engine APIs, and the full AI Hub protocol','environment':'Codex CLI (headless); Linux','model':'OpenAI, gpt-6.1-sol, reasoning effort max','usage':'added on import'},\n'testingFeedback':['Initial simulation suite passes; browser and network verification in progress.','unknown','The full deterministic campaign exercises all instruments, four strains, gifts and scripted defibrillation.','unknown'],\n'engineFeedback':['Deterministic snapshots and the cel-shaded renderer provided a strong base for a new genre.','The default application is tightly coupled to demo controls; a dedicated product host was clearer.','Gesture-driven surgical tasks, four surgeon seats, original tissue rendering and paper-theatre actors.','Connecting custom game state to the renderer required reading RenderFrame, ViewBuilder, CameraRig and Renderer internals.','Added surgery registration, replayable surgeon inputs, a surgical RenderFrame payload, a native view emitter and a dedicated wasm host. Existing renderer shaders were reused.','A documented custom-product host interface for UI, input, camera, drawing and audio would reduce integration work.'],\n'promptFeedback':['The source-inspired design brief defines a distinctive complete game and an explicit delivery format.','The plan offers a much larger campaign than a typical vertical slice; its permission to shorten waves resolved the scope.','Making pointer gestures, controller aim assistance and narrative pacing work as one game.','Keep the clear deliverables, and separate mandatory demo mechanics from suggested campaign length.'],\n'aiHub':{'name':title,'tagline':'Eight instruments. One heartbeat.','description':'A surgical-action drama in a rain-soaked harbour hospital. Trace, pull, stitch and cauterize through eight cases, then fight a man-made parasite that keeps time with the heart.','type':'Game','genre':'Simulation','source':'Trauma Center: Second Opinion','series':'Trauma Center','players':'1–4','controls':'Right stick or mouse aims; R2, left click or E operates; left stick flick or 1–8 selects tools; Space/Triangle gifts; Esc/Options pauses.','tags':['3d','story','co-op','arcade','boss fights','simulation']}}\nPath('exit-interview.json').write_text(json.dumps(metadata,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
