261105-015057__x42677a/work/Trauma-Refrain-Third-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261105-015057/engine/crates/pav_view)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_74","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nr=Path(Path('.game-path').read_text());p=r/'web/app.js';s=p.read_text().replace('if(\"'!ready||H.ended)return;loadCase(8,null);'\"','if(\"'!ready||H.ended)return;seed=H.info.seed;loadCase(8,null);'\"');s=s.replace(\\\"if(pressed(1)){backlog=\"'!backlog;draw();}'\"\\\\n  }else if(\"'!H.active)\",\"if(pressed(1)||pressed(2)){backlog=!backlog;draw();}if(pressed(3)){storyAuto=!storyAuto;draw();}'\"\\\\n  }else if(\"'!H.active)\")\np.write_text(s)\nPY\nd=$(cat .game-path); \"$d/tools/build.sh\"'","aggregated_output":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261105-015057__x42677a/work/Trauma-Refrain-Third-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261105-015057.html (5.7 MiB)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_77","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nr=Path(Path('.game-path').read_text());p=r/'engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/content/cases.json';v=json.loads(p.read_text());\nfor n,par in [(2,6900),(4,11400),(7,17400)]:v['cases'][n]['par']=par\np.write_text(json.dumps(v,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\np=r/'engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/mod.rs';s=p.read_text().replace('if self.blue{self.finish();}else{self.fail();}', 'if self.blue && self.vitals>0.{self.finish();}else{self.fail();}');p.write_text(s)\np=r/'engine/crates/pav_core/tests/surgery.rs';s=p.read_text().replace('assert_eq\"'!(g.outcome,Outcome::Won);println!(\"BALANCE'\"', 'assert_eq\"'!(g.outcome,Outcome::Won);assert!([\"S\",\"ENCORE\"].contains(&g.rank()),\"case {n}: {}\",g.rank());println!(\"BALANCE'\"');p.write_text(s)\nPY\nd=\"'$(cat .game-path); cat >> \"$d/engine/crates/pav_core/tests/surgery.rs\" <<'\"'EOF'\n#[test]\nfn code_blue_is_a_complete_survival_round(){let mut g=Surgery::new(0,false,true);play(&mut g,60*600);assert_eq\"'!(g.outcome,Outcome::Won,\"{:?}\",g.hazards);assert!(g.vitals>0.);assert!(g.wave>=10);}\nEOF\ncat > \"$d/README.md\" <<'\"'EOF'\n# Trauma Refrain: Third Opinion\n\nAn original surgical-action drama built on the Pavilion engine. Eight campaign cases follow Mara Quill and Pet Nwosu through Mercy Harbor's Night Ward. All eight instruments, four parasite movements, the Hush, Echo, Duet and cardiac resuscitation are playable. Code Blue is a four-minute survival round for one to four local or AI Hub surgeons.\n\nOpen the HTML beside this directory in Chrome or Edge, from disk or a normal static host. It includes the WASM engine, all content, its font and the unmodified AI Hub session client. WebGPU is required for the 3D theatre. WebKit displays a clear requirement notice; its mobile UI remains usable. Touch-only devices show “Controller or keyboard required”; settings and the automatic demonstration remain available.\n\nControls: mouse or right stick aims; hold left click, E, R2 or Cross to operate; digits 1–8, wheel or a left-stick flick selects an instrument. WASD/arrows move the cursor without a mouse; Shift/L2 enables precision. Space/Triangle charges a gift; release on the heartbeat. Tab/Square opens the patient chart. Both mouse buttons or L2+R2 charge the defibrillator during Code; release on the ghost beat. Wheel or L1/R1 rotates a held bone. Esc/Options pauses. Additional standard-mapped controllers join with Cross. Xbox glyphs are selectable.\n\nEvery instrument has a gesture: trace incisions, pull hooks along their axes, zigzag sutures along the advancing needle, suction pools, release the laser at 75–108%, paint gel, scan hidden objects, and release an IV dose in its mint band. In Cases 6 and 7 the Cryoprobe replaces an instrument, as labelled. Closure automatically selects Dressing. The early cases teach these gestures on the field.\n\nBuild: \"'`./tools/build.sh`. This uses Rust 1.98.1, its wasm32 target and wasm-bindgen 0.2.129 already installed here. It creates the exact root deliverable and refreshes the harness copy. `tools/bundle.py` repacks changed HTML/CSS/JS or metadata without recompiling Rust.\n\nVerify: `python3 tests/run_all.py`. Subsets: `--rust`, `--web`, `--hub`. The runner captures routine logs and prints only failures plus a one-line count. Browser logic tests run the real WASM simulation with drawing disabled; separate actual WebGPU captures verify art. `tests/visuals.py` creates the TV-size screenshots. `tests/out` contains the test evidence. No physical controller, second human, real iOS Safari or listening test was available.\n\nPause → Dev mode exposes live tuning, a bot, checkpoints, snapshots, rewind, phase/case jumps, hazard spawning and visual overlays. Content edits are documented in `engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/content/README.md`.\n\nArchitecture: `pav_core` owns deterministic surgical state and replayable four-seat input. `pav_view` draws original 3D tissue, instruments, organisms and extruded paper actors through Pavilion'\"'s renderer and procedural animation. \"'`pav_surgery` is the dedicated wasm product host; `web` supplies the controller-first shell, save format, synthesized Web Audio and AI Hub bridge. Cases and story are editable JSON. No image, model or audio files are used. Font: Barlow Condensed Semibold, SIL OFL 1.1 (licence in `vendor`). Pavilion'\"'s licence is unknown: no licence file was supplied in the source checkout.\n\nThe final About block is generated from the root \"'`exit-interview.json`. Usage stays “added on import” for the catalogue importer.\nEOF\ncat > \"$d/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/content/README.md\" <<'\"'EOF'\n# Designer guide\n\n\"'`cases.json` contains the campaign. Each case has a name, named patient and one-line life, diagnosis, surgeon, timer in seconds, par score, outcome sentence and ordered `phases`. A phase has a name, a single current objective, an urgent callout, a `plate`, optional `strain`, optional scripted `code` shock count, and `hazards`. JSON parse errors name the file, line and column.\n\nHazards use `kind`, `pos: [x,z]`, optionally `end: [x,z]`, `hidden: true` and `stage`. Gameplay bounds are x −9…9, z −4…4.1. Keep targets around x −5…5, z −2…2 for generous HUD clearance. `end` is the incision/seam endpoint, forceps pull axis or bone'\"'s snap destination. \"'`stage` advances a tumor, nodule, ember or bone'\"'s tool sequence; omit it to start at zero.\n\nKinds: \"'`incision`, `laceration`, `bleeder`, `pool`, `hook`, `shard`, `polyp`, `tumor`, `burn`, `inflammation`, `bone`, `nodule`, `sac`, `ember`, `tether`, `soloist`, `tendril`, `dressing`. Their tools, drain, progress, gesture and misuse rules are in `Hazard::tool` and `Surgery::operate`. A phase advances only when every task is cleared and scripted shocks are complete. A pool reveals hidden objects below it when suctioned. Scanner reveals hidden objects for eight seconds. Completed seams retain visible stitches. Every phase is a retry checkpoint.\n\nPlate keys: `forearm`, `abdomen`, `bowel`, `chest`, `lung`, `liver`, `femur`, `pericardium`, `heart`; Code Blue reuses the forearm field. Plates are procedural in `pav_view/src/surgery.rs`; extend `height` and `color_plate` for new organs. Strain keys: `introit`, `lacrimosa`, `dies`, `furnace`, `libera`. They enable beat-driven movement, bursting sacs, fever and heat rings. Use consecutive phases for shell divisions, eye windows, furnace reveals or the Soloist. Core coverage records each phase, tool, strain, hazard and gift.\n\nStory authoring source: the product directory'\"'s \"'`tools/make_story.py`. Each line is `Speaker|Dialogue`; scenes name the set and two actors. Run that script to regenerate `web/story.json`, or edit JSON directly (then do not regenerate). Each JSON line has `who`, `text`, `expr`, `left`, `right`, `set`. Speakers are Mara, Pet, Bashir, Teddy, Voss, Vane. Expressions: neutral, alarmed, stern, soft. Sets: corridor, gallery, gala, ward, depot, scrub, recovery, ship. Actor silhouettes, colours, expressions and procedural animation are in `pav_view/src/surgery.rs::actor` and `theatre`. Music, cues and voice timbres are in `web/audio.js`.\n\nTuning: all live variables are in `Tune` in core `surgery/mod.rs`. Pause → Dev mode changes them immediately, can keep the simulation Live, or let the Bot operate. Reset All restores constructor defaults. Each dev slider shows its default. Use the case/phase page to jump, then save a snapshot before testing a hazard. The browser embeds content; rebuild with `tools/build.sh` after editing case data or Rust. Repack with `tools/bundle.py` after story or shell edits. Native `pav load scene=surgery/case/3` reads cases from disk at load, so no Rust rebuild is needed for data-only tuning. `pav play scene=surgery/campaign bot=true seeds=10` plays the complete campaign. Build the native CLI with `cargo build --locked -p pav_tools --bin pav` from the engine directory.\n\nRun `python3 tests/run_all.py --rust` from the product directory to check content, tools, scores, all cases, the campaign, survival, snapshots and replays. The same command with no flags adds browser and hub checks. Calibrate `par` from the expert bot'\"'s measured score, then adjust timer and drain for human pacing. To add a new gesture or strain, update its bot planner too; campaign coverage should prove it can be completed.\nEOF\ncd \\\"\"'$d/engine\"; CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=6 cargo test --locked -p pav_core --test surgery > ../test-core.log 2>&1'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
