{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_114","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('exit-interview.json');v=json.loads(p.read_text())\nv['sourceInformation']['testing']='Headless Rust and WASM campaign, gestures, controller/touch stand-ins, audio analyser, saves, checkpoints, UI bounds, AI Hub harness and two-copy synchronization; 24 responsive captures in Chromium, Firefox and WebKit. Real WebGPU art checked in Chromium. WebKit checks its requirement message; real iOS Safari, physical controllers, a second human and listening review were unavailable.'\nv['testingFeedback']=[\n'Five product issues were found and fixed: idle-controller input arbitration, touch-attract exit, chart contrast, overflowing panels, and an AI partner that could carry an idle player. Two test assertions also needed correction.',\n'Two were game breaking for affected inputs or screens: an idle pad could overwrite mouse/keyboard actions, and low-contrast charts hid essential briefing text.',\n'Real mouse and controller gesture tests with both connected. They found an input failure the deterministic bot could not expose; the full campaign test separately proved feature coverage.',\n'Repeating identical deterministic bot case runs added little after snapshots and replays had been verified.'\n]\nv['engineFeedback']=[\n'The deterministic Game hook, snapshots and cel-shaded WebGPU renderer made a new genre testable and gave surgical instruments useful lighting and shadows.',\n'The stock application owns demo menus, camera controls and touch input. I used a dedicated product host rather than trying to adapt that flow. Adding frame/input fields also required updating other constructors.',\n'The physical gesture evaluator and replayable four-surgeon state: tracing, extraction axes, stitch crossings, timed heat and doses, gifts and resuscitation.',\n'Custom game presentation required reading RenderFrame, ViewBuilder, CameraRig, Renderer and input-tool internals. UI, camera, audio and rendering have separate integration points.',\n'Registered surgery; extended InputFrame and RenderFrame; added the procedural surgery view, extruded paper actors, a native surgical input command and a dedicated wasm host. The original renderer and sim-driven animation remain the base; the browser shell and synthesized audio use HTML and Web Audio.',\n'A documented per-game product interface owning camera, input, UI, audio and custom scene emission would remove much of the integration work.'\n]\nv['promptFeedback']=[\n'The combination of a distinctive source-inspired design, explicit delivery format and editable-data requirement gave the game a clear identity and finish line.',\n'The plan describes an hour-long campaign while the task asks for a vertical slice. Its permission to shorten waves made the scope practical without dropping mechanics.',\n'Making mouse gestures, controller precision, the heartbeat clock, story pacing and shared-world co-op work together as one game.',\n'Keep the concrete deliverables and testing rules; distinguish required demo mechanics from suggested campaign length, and provide a small custom-product engine host example.'\n]\np.write_text(json.dumps(v,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nr=Path(Path('.game-path').read_text());p=r/'tools/bundle.py';s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"subprocess.run(['wasm-bindgen','--target','web','--no-typescript','--out-dir',str(build),'--out-name','surgery',str(wasm)],check=True,capture_output=True)\\\",\\\"if wasm.exists():\\\\n subprocess.run(['wasm-bindgen','--target','web','--no-typescript','--out-dir',str(build),'--out-name','surgery',str(wasm)],check=True,capture_output=True)\\\\nelse:\\\\n assert (build/'surgery.js').exists() and (build/'surgery_bg.wasm').exists(), 'Run tools/build.sh first'\\\")\np.write_text(s)\np=r/'tests/run_all.py';s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"'--test','surgery']\\\",\\\"'--test','surgery','--test','games']\\\");s=s.replace(\\\"m=re.search(r'test result: .*?(\\\\\\\\d+) passed; (\\\\\\\\d+) failed',text)\\\\n if m:passed+=int(m[1]);failed+=int(m[2])\\\", \\\"matches=re.findall(r'test result: .*?(\\\\\\\\d+) passed; (\\\\\\\\d+) failed',text)\\\\n if matches:\\\\n  for a,b in matches:passed+=int(a);failed+=int(b)\\\")\np.write_text(s)\nPY\nd=\"'$(cat .game-path); python3 -m py_compile \"$d/tests/run_all.py\" \"$d/tools/bundle.py\"; tail -35 \"$d/test-core.log\"; tail -6 \"$d/build-web.log\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_114","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('exit-interview.json');v=json.loads(p.read_text())\nv['sourceInformation']['testing']='Headless Rust and WASM campaign, gestures, controller/touch stand-ins, audio analyser, saves, checkpoints, UI bounds, AI Hub harness and two-copy synchronization; 24 responsive captures in Chromium, Firefox and WebKit. Real WebGPU art checked in Chromium. WebKit checks its requirement message; real iOS Safari, physical controllers, a second human and listening review were unavailable.'\nv['testingFeedback']=[\n'Five product issues were found and fixed: idle-controller input arbitration, touch-attract exit, chart contrast, overflowing panels, and an AI partner that could carry an idle player. Two test assertions also needed correction.',\n'Two were game breaking for affected inputs or screens: an idle pad could overwrite mouse/keyboard actions, and low-contrast charts hid essential briefing text.',\n'Real mouse and controller gesture tests with both connected. They found an input failure the deterministic bot could not expose; the full campaign test separately proved feature coverage.',\n'Repeating identical deterministic bot case runs added little after snapshots and replays had been verified.'\n]\nv['engineFeedback']=[\n'The deterministic Game hook, snapshots and cel-shaded WebGPU renderer made a new genre testable and gave surgical instruments useful lighting and shadows.',\n'The stock application owns demo menus, camera controls and touch input. I used a dedicated product host rather than trying to adapt that flow. Adding frame/input fields also required updating other constructors.',\n'The physical gesture evaluator and replayable four-surgeon state: tracing, extraction axes, stitch crossings, timed heat and doses, gifts and resuscitation.',\n'Custom game presentation required reading RenderFrame, ViewBuilder, CameraRig, Renderer and input-tool internals. UI, camera, audio and rendering have separate integration points.',\n'Registered surgery; extended InputFrame and RenderFrame; added the procedural surgery view, extruded paper actors, a native surgical input command and a dedicated wasm host. The original renderer and sim-driven animation remain the base; the browser shell and synthesized audio use HTML and Web Audio.',\n'A documented per-game product interface owning camera, input, UI, audio and custom scene emission would remove much of the integration work.'\n]\nv['promptFeedback']=[\n'The combination of a distinctive source-inspired design, explicit delivery format and editable-data requirement gave the game a clear identity and finish line.',\n'The plan describes an hour-long campaign while the task asks for a vertical slice. Its permission to shorten waves made the scope practical without dropping mechanics.',\n'Making mouse gestures, controller precision, the heartbeat clock, story pacing and shared-world co-op work together as one game.',\n'Keep the concrete deliverables and testing rules; distinguish required demo mechanics from suggested campaign length, and provide a small custom-product engine host example.'\n]\np.write_text(json.dumps(v,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nr=Path(Path('.game-path').read_text());p=r/'tools/bundle.py';s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"subprocess.run(['wasm-bindgen','--target','web','--no-typescript','--out-dir',str(build),'--out-name','surgery',str(wasm)],check=True,capture_output=True)\\\",\\\"if wasm.exists():\\\\n subprocess.run(['wasm-bindgen','--target','web','--no-typescript','--out-dir',str(build),'--out-name','surgery',str(wasm)],check=True,capture_output=True)\\\\nelse:\\\\n assert (build/'surgery.js').exists() and (build/'surgery_bg.wasm').exists(), 'Run tools/build.sh first'\\\")\np.write_text(s)\np=r/'tests/run_all.py';s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"'--test','surgery']\\\",\\\"'--test','surgery','--test','games']\\\");s=s.replace(\\\"m=re.search(r'test result: .*?(\\\\\\\\d+) passed; (\\\\\\\\d+) failed',text)\\\\n if m:passed+=int(m[1]);failed+=int(m[2])\\\", \\\"matches=re.findall(r'test result: .*?(\\\\\\\\d+) passed; (\\\\\\\\d+) failed',text)\\\\n if matches:\\\\n  for a,b in matches:passed+=int(a);failed+=int(b)\\\")\np.write_text(s)\nPY\nd=\"'$(cat .game-path); python3 -m py_compile \"$d/tests/run_all.py\" \"$d/tools/bundle.py\"; tail -35 \"$d/test-core.log\"; tail -6 \"$d/build-web.log\"'","aggregated_output":"   Compiling pav_core v0.1.0 (/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261105-015057__x42677a/work/Trauma-Refrain-Third-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261105-015057/engine/crates/pav_core)\n    Finished `test` profile [optimized + debuginfo] target(s) in 1m 22s\n     Running tests/games.rs (target/debug/deps/games-884d29e9293fd36a)\n\nrunning 4 tests\ntest game_keys_name_one_scene_each ... ok\ntest snapshots_rewind_and_replays_are_exact ... ok\ntest standing_still_gets_caught ... ok\ntest the_starter_bot_wins_on_ten_seeds ... ok\n\ntest result: ok. 4 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 1.19s\n\n     Running tests/surgery.rs (target/debug/deps/surgery-6e1ac209a8f6f04b)\n\nrunning 12 tests\ntest careless_extraction_is_sloppy_and_tears_tissue ... ok\ntest wrong_tool_and_checkpoint_are_real ... ok\ntest code_blue_is_a_complete_survival_round ... ok\ntest iv_release_and_shock_timing_change_the_patient ... ok\ntest editable_content_is_complete ... ok\ntest expert_balance_measurements ... ok\ntest echo_does_not_steal_a_fourth_human_seat ... ok\ntest every_case_is_winnable ... ok\ntest idle_loses_every_case ... ok\ntest snapshots_and_replays_are_exact ... ok\ntest campaign_exercises_the_whole_language ... ok\ntest the_partner_cannot_win_for_an_idle_lead_surgeon ... ok\n\ntest result: ok. 12 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.12s\n\n   Compiling pav_core v0.1.0 (/home/m